// @id 01M5AVRFY2ZME86820F3HFZZ1D model=basic-example
q: What is **Kirchhoff's First Law / the Junction Rule / Kirchhoff's Current Law**?
a: It states that the sum of currents entering a junction equals the sum of currents leaving the same junction. $$\sum{I_{IN}} = \sum{I_{OUT}} = \sum{I} = 0$$

// @id 01M5AVRFY35MW1ZGBZ4JAC5T51 model=basic-example
q: What is **Kirchhoff's Second Law / Kirchhoff's Voltage Law**?
a: It states that the algebraic sum of all potential differences (voltages) around any closed loop in a circuit is zero. $$\sum{V} = 0$$

